# Keep shell scripts LF so the bash shebang runs when a macOS/Linux user downloads the
# installer via `curl … | bash`, even from a Windows (core.autocrlf=true) checkout.
/install.sh eol=lf
*.sh text eol=lf

# Vendored minified runtime (Mermaid): keep byte-exact — EOL/text normalization could
# corrupt the pinned library. Treat as-is.
src/Charter.Core/assets/mermaid.min.js -text

# Per-author review logs (docs/plans/03-git-mediated-team-review.md §3). Both settings are built into git,
# so there is nothing to install. `merge=union` is an OPTIMIZATION, never a correctness dependency: without
# it a same-author-two-branches divergence degrades to a loud CONFLICT that a human resolves, which the fold
# survives. `text eol=lf` is NOT cosmetic — without it a CRLF-writing teammate forks every line and union
# keeps both copies (reproduced in the merge spike). The `**/` prefix is required: `*.charter.review/*.jsonl`
# alone matches only at the repository root.
**/*.charter.review/*.jsonl merge=union text eol=lf
